    "math_academy_id": "q-31871",
    "knowledge_point_id": "8a4b135f-df0d-5443-bb93-796f32c380c6",
    "knowledge_point": "Identifying the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix Calculated Using Row Operations",
    "problem": "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $B$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${B}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "We write down $B$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $B$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${B}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{B}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
