    "reasoning": "All 16 selected answers agree with their own captured worked solutions and the mathematics. q-32026: the coefficient determinant is 31, giving (x,y)=(3/31,-8/31). q-102705: the determinant is 2, giving (x,y)=(1/2,1). Both selected matrix products represent these solutions. q-79754: multiplying by y on the original domain y≠0 gives y′−2y=x², a first-order linear ODE; the other choices retain nonlinear dependence on y. q-75503: swapping rows and subtracting three times the new first row gives lower-left entries 3, −6, and 0 respectively, so only C becomes the identity. q-43000: only B becomes the identity after swapping rows and halving the first row. q-131380: the missing operation is R₂:=−R₂, giving the selected inverse. q-31871: the missing operation is R₂:=(1/5)R₂, giving the selected inverse. q-31945: adding 2R₁ to R₂ eliminates −2; later adding (4/3)R₂ to R₁ eliminates −4/3. q-31872: dividing R₂ by 3 makes its pivot 1; adding (5/2)R₂ to R₁ eliminates −5/2. q-71189 and q-71190: delete row 2 and column 3, and row 3 and column 4, respectively, then take the remaining determinant. q-32793 and q-130904: delete the indicated row and column; both cofactor signs are positive because 1+5 and 5+1 are even. q-131096: first-row expansion gives −(6·4·2)=−48. q-36045: expansion gives 2((-3)·5−4·4)=−62. q-332552: the particular solution −x²+x−2 has derivative −2x+1, so y′+y=−x²−x−1; adding Ae^(−x) gives the selected general solution. No submitted grade or earlier answer was supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
